{"reference":"Psalms 129","book":"Psalms","chapter":129,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Songs of Ascents","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 129 stands within Psalms 120–134, a collection oriented toward worship. These surrounding psalms preserve memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, and meditation on Torah. This wider setting places Psalm 129’s communal voice among varied expressions of worship and remembrance.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_129_4e643a625866afe72c8a9abf"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}